# USER ROLE MASTERY: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2

> Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) governs every action in the system.
> Firebase custom claims are the single source of truth. No exceptions.

---

## 1. CANONICAL ROLE TAXONOMY

### General Platform Roles
| Role | Custom Claim | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `superAdmin` | `{ superAdmin: true }` | Full system access; can manage all roles |
| `admin` | `{ admin: true }` | Manage content, users, settings |
| `moderator` | `{ moderator: true }` | Content-only admin; no user management |
| `member` | `{ member: true }` | Authenticated standard user |
| `guest` | *(no claim)* | Unauthenticated / public access |

### Ecommerce Extension Roles
| Role | Custom Claim | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `vendor` | `{ vendor: true, vendorId: "v_xxx" }` | Manages own store/products |
| `distributor` | `{ distributor: true, distributorId: "d_xxx" }` | B2B bulk buyer / reseller |
| `affiliate` | `{ affiliate: true, affiliateId: "a_xxx" }` | Commission-based referral partner |
| `support` | `{ support: true }` | Read-only across orders/users; no write |
| `fulfillment` | `{ fulfillment: true }` | Mark orders shipped/fulfilled only |
| `customer` | `{ customer: true }` | Standard buyer account |

**Rule**: Roles are NOT stored as a string field. They are individual boolean claims to support multi-role users.

---

## 2. FIREBASE CUSTOM CLAIMS — The Source of Truth

```typescript
// ✅ Admin SDK — server-only (Cloud Function)
import { auth } from 'firebase-admin';

// GRANT a role
export async function grantRole(uid: string, role: string, meta?: Record<string, string>) {
  const user = await auth().getUser(uid);
  const existing = user.customClaims ?? {};
  await auth().setCustomUserClaims(uid, {
    ...existing,
    [role]: true,
    ...meta, // e.g. vendorId, distributorId
  });
}

// REVOKE a role
export async function revokeRole(uid: string, role: string) {
  const user = await auth().getUser(uid);
  const claims = { ...(user.customClaims ?? {}) };
  delete claims[role];
  await auth().setCustomUserClaims(uid, claims);
}
```

**Critical rules:**
- Claims are set server-side ONLY via Admin SDK — never from the client.
- After `setCustomUserClaims`, user MUST refresh their ID token to get new claims.
- Force token refresh: `await auth.currentUser?.getIdToken(true)`.
- Max custom claims payload: **1000 bytes**. Keep payloads lean.

